2. **Construct the integrand**: Multiply $ u(r) $ by the number density $ \frac{N}{V} $ and spherical volume element $ 4\pi r^2 \, dr $ to form $ U_{\text{avg}} = \int_{d}^{\infty} -\epsilon \left( \frac{d}{r} \right)^6 \cdot \frac{N}{V} \cdot 4\pi r^2 \, dr $.  
3. **Simplify and evaluate the integral**: Reduce the integrand to $ -\frac{4\pi \epsilon d^6 N}{V} \int_{d}^{\infty} r^{-4} \, dr $, compute $ \int_{d}^{\infty} r^{-4} \, dr = \frac{1}{3d^3} $, yielding $ U_{\text{avg}} = -\frac{4\pi \epsilon d^3 N}{3V} $.  
