3. Expand and simplify to $ 3h^2 - 66h + 265 = 0 $. 
4. Solve using the quadratic formula: $ h = \frac{66 \pm \sqrt{66^2 - 4 \cdot 3 \cdot 265}}{6} $. 
5. Select the smaller root $ h = \frac{33 - 7\sqrt{6}}{3} $, rewrite $ 7\sqrt{6} $ as $ \sqrt{294} $, yielding $ \frac{33 - \sqrt{294}}{3} $. 
6. Sum $ r = 33 $, $ s = 294 $, $ t = 3 $ to get $ 330 $.
