For part (2), the core principle is homogenization theory for kinetic equations. Integrating the joint density PDE over velocity gives the spatial marginal density $ m(t, x) $, whose evolution is governed by an effective diffusion equation $ m_t = m_{xx} $ due to velocity dispersion. On a circle with periodic boundary conditions, solutions to this diffusion equation converge to uniformity as $ t \to \infty $.

