   - The image is the centralizer of the swap automorphism in $ \text{GL}(2, 3) $, which has order 4.
   - The kernel consists of automorphisms acting trivially on $ H $, corresponding to elements of $ H $ fixed by the swap (i.e., $ (c, c) $ for $ c \in \mathbb{Z}/3\mathbb{Z} $), giving kernel size 3.
4. Conclude $ |\text{Aut } G| = 4 \times 3 = 12 $, which is less than $ |\text{Aut } H| = 48 $.
5. Verify $ H $ is normal in $ G $ (as the unique Sylow 3-subgroup) and finalize the example.
