2. Express the partial sum $\sum_{n=0}^N \mathrm{Arccot}(n^2 + n + 1)$ as a telescoping series: $\mathrm{Arccot}(0) - \mathrm{Arccot}(N+1)$. 
3. Evaluate the limit of the partial sum as $N \to \infty$, noting $\lim_{N \to \infty} \mathrm{Arccot}(N+1) = 0$ and $\mathrm{Arccot}(0) = \pi/2$. 
4. Conclude the infinite sum equals $\pi/2$.
