2. Use the **hydrostatic equation** ($ dP/dz = -\rho g $) and **ideal gas law** ($ \rho = P/(R_d T) $) to relate $ dP/dz $ to $ T $.
3. Express saturation mixing ratio $ w_s $ via the **Clausius-Clapeyron equation**: $ w_s \approx \varepsilon e_s / P $, where $ e_s = e_0 \exp\left[-\frac{L_v}{R_v}\left(\frac{1}{T_{\text{parcel}}} - \frac{1}{T_0}\right)\right] $, and differentiate $ w_s $ with respect to $ T_{\text{parcel}} $.
