- *Calculation Traps*: Incorrectly assuming the period of \( 2^n \mod 125 \) is 20 (it is 100). Failing to account for the linear term \( n \) in \( 2^n \equiv n \pmod{125} \), which requires solving a congruence with both exponential and linear components.
