The starting toss determines the relationship between transitions and runs: if the sequence starts with T and ends with H (even runs), then $ \text{HT} = R_H - 1 $ and $ \text{TH} = R_T $. The number of valid sequences is the product of compositions for head runs ($ \binom{N_H - 1}{R_H - 1} $) and tail runs ($ \binom{N_T - 1}{R_T - 1} $) via stars and bars.

