2. Calculate the circumradius \( R = \frac{20 \times 20 \times 24}{4 \times \text{Area}} \). 
3. Determine the pyramid height \( h = \sqrt{25^2 - R^2} \). 
4. Apply the volume formula \( \frac{1}{3} \times \text{Area} \times h \), simplify to \( m\sqrt{n} \), and compute \( m + n \). This ensures all steps are grounded in geometric principles and avoids critical errors.
</think>
